## Conventions

- Commit messages, PR titles and branch names follow Conventional Commits and Conventional Branch
  (`feature/add-thing`, `bugfix/fix-thing`, `chore/update-thing`). CI lints PR titles and branch names.
- Run before pushing: `cargo fmt --all --check`, `cargo clippy --locked --all-targets -- -D warnings`, `cargo test --locked`.
- The minimum supported Rust version is `[[ rust_version ]]`; CI builds on it, so keep `rust-version` in `Cargo.toml` honest.
- Releases are automatic: merge the release-please PR. Never tag by hand. See `REPOSITORY_SETUP.md`.
- One-time GitHub settings (immutable releases, the `publish` environment[% if include_crates_publish %], crates.io trusted publishing[% endif %]) are in `REPOSITORY_SETUP.md`.
- Pin every GitHub Action by commit SHA (zizmor enforces it) and keep `permissions:` minimal.
